# Vercel Web Analytics Implementation

Successfully installed and configured Vercel Web Analytics for the CodeStats Next.js application.

## Changes Made

### 1. Package Installation
- **File**: `web/package.json`
- **Action**: Added `@vercel/analytics` v2.0.1 as a dependency
- **Command**: `npm install @vercel/analytics`
- **Lock File**: Updated `package-lock.json` to reflect the new dependency

### 2. Analytics Integration
- **File**: `web/src/app/layout.tsx`
- **Actions**:
  - Added import statement: `import { Analytics } from "@vercel/analytics/next";`
  - Added `<Analytics />` component at the end of the body section, after the Providers wrapper
  
### 3. Implementation Details

Following the official Vercel documentation (fetched from https://vercel.com/docs/analytics/quickstart), the Analytics component was added to the root layout file as recommended for Next.js App Router applications.

The component is placed at the end of the body tag to ensure it doesn't interfere with the existing layout structure and renders after all main content.

## Verification

✅ **Build Test**: Successfully ran `npm run build` - no errors introduced
✅ **Linting**: Ran `npm run lint` on layout.tsx - no linting errors in our changes
✅ **Type Checking**: TypeScript compilation passed without issues
✅ **Lock Files**: package-lock.json properly updated

## Post-Deployment Steps

To complete the setup, the project maintainer should:
1. Deploy the application to Vercel
2. Navigate to the Vercel dashboard → Analytics section
3. Click "Enable" to activate Web Analytics for the project
4. Analytics data will start appearing within a few days of user visits

## Technical Notes

- Framework: Next.js 16.2.10 (App Router)
- Package Manager: npm
- Analytics Package Version: @vercel/analytics@2.0.1
- No breaking changes or conflicts with existing dependencies
- The Analytics component is React Server Component compatible and works seamlessly with the existing Providers wrapper
